 {
  "coord": "14:55",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "invention",
  "note": "'Taste most palates theirs' rendered as 'loudest voice most pleases their taste', which is not in the source.",
  "replacement": "CORIOLANUS. \"Shall\"? Oh, good but most unwise patricians! You grave but reckless senators, have you let the Hydra, the many-headed monster, choose an officer for itself? He is only the horn and the noise of the monster, yet with his commanding \"shall\" he has the nerve to say he'll turn your river into a ditch and make your channel his own. If he has power, then lower your heads in shame at your ignorance. If he has none, wake up from your dangerous softness. If you are wise, don't act like common fools. If you are not, let them have cushions beside you. You are plebeians if they are senators. And they are no less than that when your votes and theirs are blended, and the strongest flavor is theirs. They choose their magistrate, and he is the kind of man who sets his \"shall,\" his popular \"shall,\" against a more serious bench than ever frowned in Greece. By Jove himself, it makes the consuls look base! And my soul aches to think how soon, when two authorities are up and neither is supreme, confusion may enter the gap between them and make one swallow the other."
 },
