 {
  "coord": "14:160",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "reversal",
  "note": "'To lose it by his country' becomes losing it 'to' his country, which reads as giving it, not having it taken by Rome.",
  "replacement": "MENENIUS. Oh, he's a limb that has only a disease. Cutting it off would be deadly, but curing it is easy. What has he done to Rome that deserves death? He killed our enemies. The blood he has lost, and I dare swear it is many an ounce more than what he has left, he spilled for his country. And to have what is left lost at his own country's hands would be, for all of us who do it and allow it, a brand of shame until the end of the world."
 },
