 {
  "coord": "15:28",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "reversal",
  "note": "The head corrects the stout heart; the candidate makes the listener correct the head.",
  "replacement": "VOLUMNIA. Please now, my son, go to them with this cap in your hand. Hold it out as far as this, and here stand before them, with your knee kissing the stones. In such business action is eloquence, and the eyes of the ignorant are more learned than their ears. Wave your head, which often corrects your stout heart this way, and be humble now, like the ripest mulberry that won't bear handling. Or say to them that you are their soldier, bred in battles, and you lack the soft manner that you admit would suit you to use, as they have a right to claim it, when asking for their good love. But say that from now on you will, in truth, make yourself theirs, as far as you have power and person."
 },
